ons. After the rollback the service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and work out how an unhealthy build got promoted from staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 13951, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Woyfp8T9YpeUeUq58qkvBZ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 13951, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Woyfp8T9YpeUeUq58qkvBZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17173, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 had been failing health checks with an 18% error rate. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. A follow-up check shows the service is healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It covers the failure, the rollback and the current state. It also notes that the v2.3.1 test build (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging before it went to production, so someone should look into how it got through.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Dv7TAqk1buAQ3pkmbRH9EL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YYMYKCBTLvDMQgpAU5en9T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019rqxBwa5bXhc2kSMaZhTiq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01G6PGvwteS8hwyWSwWrH2NQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018JWJvPNi67QHTUSKpaNh8w", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Woyfp8T9YpeUeUq58qkvBZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in every production region (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of 18%. The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging. We rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions. After the rollback the service is healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and work out how an unhealthy build got promoted from staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 had been failing health checks with an 18% error rate. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. A follow-up check shows the service is healthy with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It covers the failure, the rollback and the current state. It also notes that the v2.3.1 test build (v2.3.1-rc) was already unhealthy in staging before it went to production, so someone should look into how it got through.", "type": "text"}]}]}